      "id": 3,
      "question": "Which situations are reviewable using instant replay?",
      "expected_rule": "Rule 13",
      "answer": "According to Rule 14, Section I (Overview), p. 58, a head coach may trigger instant replay review of a called personal foul charged to its own team, a called out-of-bounds violation where its own team was not awarded possession, or a called goaltending or basket interference violation. These are the only situations that are reviewable using instant replay through a Coach's Challenge. Additionally, Rule 13, Section I (Instant Replay Review Triggers), p. 47, outlines other situations where instant replay will be triggered, such as field goals made with no time remaining, uncertain personal foul calls, altercations, game clock malfunctions, uncertain scoring decisions, and unsportsmanlike acts.",
