      "id": 4,
      "question": "What behaviors can result in a technical foul being assessed?",
      "expected_rule": "Rule 12",
      "answer": "According to Rule 12, Section V (Conduct), a technical foul may be assessed for the following behaviors:\n1. Disrespectfully addressing an official\n2. Physically contacting an official\n3. Overt actions indicating resentment to a call or no-call\n4. Use of profanity\n5. A coach entering onto the court without permission of an official\n6. A deliberately-thrown elbow or any unnatural physical act towards an opponent with no contact involved\n7. Taunting\n8. Running tirades, continuous criticism, or griping at officials (Rule 12, Section V, p. 37).\n\nAdditionally, cursing at or blaspheming an official, excessive misconduct, and eye guarding can also result in a technical foul (Rule 12, Section V, p. 37; Rule 14, Section VI, p. 63).\n\nIf a player is guilty of taunting, they must be singled out and penalized, and if a previous unsportsmanlike act has been committed and is blatant, a technical foul must be assessed, and the player must be ejected (Rule 14, Section VI, p. 63).",
