      "answer": "According to Rule 5, Section VI (Timeouts – Mandatory/Team), p. 17, each team is entitled to seven (7) charged timeouts during regulation play. Each team is limited to no more than four (4) timeouts in the fourth period. In overtime periods, each team is allowed two (2) team timeouts. Therefore, a team receives a total of seven timeouts during a regulation NBA game.",
