      "question": "How many free throws are awarded for different types of personal fouls?",
      "expected_rule": "Rule 8",
      "answer": "According to Rule 12, Section IX (p. 46), punching fouls result in two free throw attempts being awarded. According to Rule 12, Section XI (p. 47), transition take fouls result in one free throw attempt being awarded, but if the foul is flagrant or punching, two free throw attempts are awarded. Away-from-the-play fouls, as per Rule 12, Section X (p. 46), result in one free throw attempt being awarded, but if the foul is flagrant or punching, two free throw attempts are awarded. Offensive fouls, as per Rule 12, Section VII (p. 45), do not result in free throw attempts unless the foul is punching or flagrant, in which case two free throw attempts are awarded.",
